.ai/10_state/current-state.md:1635:**AI Ask Quota And Audit Fail-Closed Deployed (2026-06-04):** Main commit `e48eb0f` fixes the Codex Security finding `AI Ask endpoint lacks quota and fails open on audit` for the disabled-by-default Ask Flip path. If `ARCHESTIMATOR_AI_ENABLED=true` is ever set, `/api/ai/ask` now checks durable quota in `security_rate_limit_events` before workspace context reads or provider spend, returns HTTP 429 with `Retry-After` on quota denial, returns HTTP 503 when quota storage is unavailable, requires a `started` audit upsert before DeepSeek is called, withholds successful provider output unless the `completed` audit update succeeds, and requires failed-audit persistence for read-context/provider failures before returning their normal error response. Verification passed the focused AI route/audit suite (5 files / 66 tests), `bun run type-check`, `bun run lint` with 12 existing warnings / 0 errors, `bun run build`, `git diff --check`, and GitNexus staged detect-changes LOW risk with 0 affected processes. Vercel production deploy `DEPLOYMENT_ID_PLACEHOLDER` is Ready and aliased to `www.archestimator.com`, `archestimator.com`, and `archestimator.vercel.app`; hosted smoke returned HTTP 200 from `https://www.archestimator.com/api/health`, apex health redirected to `www`, and signed-out `POST https://www.archestimator.com/api/ai/ask` returned HTTP 404 with `{"error":"AI is disabled for closed beta."}`. Proof artifact: `.ai/09_archive/store/2026-06-02-mvp-closed-beta-manual-proof/ai-ask-quota-audit-fail-closed-2026-06-04.json`. Codex Security rescan/closure remains pending, and no real enabled-AI hosted provider/audit-row smoke was run because AI remains intentionally off for the cheaper closed beta.
.ai/10_state/current-state.md:1637:**Project Image Storage Hardened In Linked Supabase And Production (2026-06-04):** Repo code commit `ea4aa95` fixes the Codex Security finding `Project images are uploaded to a public listable bucket` by moving project cover uploads from the public `component-images` bucket to a private `project-images` bucket, returning same-origin `/api/projects/images?path=...` route URLs, serving images only after authenticated project-access checks, stripping project-image route/storage URLs from public share snapshots, and removing the public `project-images` Next image remote pattern. Linked Supabase migration `20260603222628_private_project_image_storage.sql` created/locked the private bucket and excluded `/project-images/` paths from public component-image reads; follow-up migration `20260603224800_qualify_project_image_storage_policies.sql` repaired the project-image policy predicates with explicit `storage.objects.name` qualification and full UUID checks. Live readback now shows `project-images.public=false`, `component-images` project-image subtree object count `0`, private project-image object count `6`, project metadata using private route URLs `3`, component-bucket project-image metadata `0`, both migration versions recorded, and project-image read/insert/update/delete policies present. Cache-busted old public object access returns HTTP 400 `Object not found`, direct public `project-images` bucket access returns HTTP 400, and unauthenticated same-origin image-route access redirects to `/login`. Vercel production deploy `DEPLOYMENT_ID_PLACEHOLDER` is Ready and aliased to `www.archestimator.com`, `archestimator.com`, and `archestimator.vercel.app`; post-migration health returned HTTP 200 from `https://www.archestimator.com/api/health` and apex redirects to `www`. Proof artifact: `.ai/09_archive/store/2026-06-02-mvp-closed-beta-manual-proof/project-images-private-storage-2026-06-04.json`. Codex Security rescan/closure remains pending, and closed-beta launch-ready language remains blocked by remaining findings plus hosted Google OAuth/provider/manual proof gaps.
