timator.com/api/health`, apex health redirected to `www`, `/login` returned HTTP 200, and signed-out `/workshop` returned HTTP 307 to `/login?next=%2Fworkshop`. Codex Security refresh after deploy remains stale: `Global comment circuit breaker can be tripped by bad UUIDs` still appears in the 42-row Findings table against old commit `2d93eef`. Closed-beta launch-ready language remains blocked until Codex Security rescans/closes or owner-accepts remaining findings plus hosted Google OAuth/provider/manual proof gaps.
.ai/10_state/current-state.md:1679:**Share Tree Designation DoS Hardened And Deployed (2026-06-04):** Main commit `d5e2f72` bounds public share-tree designation parsing before split/allocation in `src/lib/share/reconstruct-share-tree.ts`: designation text is sliced to 2048 characters, split output is capped to `MAX_DEPTH + 1` segments, individual node labels are capped to 120 characters, and hostile over-depth rows are retained with correct totals instead of being dropped. Regression tests in `tests/vitest/share/reconstruct-share-tree.test.ts` first failed on the old behavior (row count `0` for an 80-segment designation and an uncapped 2000-character label), then passed after the fix. Verification passed `bunx vitest run tests/vitest/share/reconstruct-share-tree.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` (23 tests), the focused share/publication suite `bunx vitest run tests/vitest/share/reconstruct-share-tree.test.ts tests/vitest/project-publication-page.test.tsx tests/vitest/project-publication-snapshot.test.ts tests/vitest/project-publication-route.test.ts tests/vitest/share/share-page-get-routes-contract.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` (5 files / 64 tests), `bun run type-check`, `bun run lint` with 12 existing warnings / 0 errors, `git diff --check`, `bun run build`, GitNexus impact/detect-changes LOW risk, and code-review-graph detect_changes risk `0.55` with 0 affected flows. A direct adversarial Bun probe with 100,000 delimiter segments returned in about 5.8ms with 21 nodes, max depth 20, rowCount 1, and total 777. Vercel production deploy `DEPLOYMENT_ID_PLACEHOLDER` is Ready and aliased to `www.archestimator.com`, `archestimator.com`, and `archestimator.vercel.app`; post-deploy smoke returned HTTP 200 from `https://www.archestimator.com/api/health`, apex health redirected to `www`, `/login` returned HTTP 200, signed-out `/workshop` returned HTTP 307 to `/login?next=%2Fworkshop`, homepage title was `Archestimator | Quote, Proposal & Estimate Workspace`, and homepage HTML had no Speed In