iews and existing estimate Area Nodes, and can use normalized/capped provider `searchTerms` as row-planning hints against already-retrieved scoped component matches. Generic condo Draft reads use the full bounded package search vocabulary so wardrobe, kitchen/cabinet/millwork, water-closet, lavatory/basin/sink/faucet, living, dining, furniture, console, table, sofa, chair, pendant, lounge, light, fixture, paint, tile, bathroom, sanitary, finish, and general data can be discovered even when the user does not name each component. The provider may receive bounded portfolio project labels, current project estimate summaries, and ID-free comparable package summaries; when route context resolves a current project/estimate, it may also receive provider-safe current project name, estimate summary, current area names/paths, and compact current area rows. Raw project/estimate/node/row ids and client/location details are not forwarded. Historical estimate rows, comparable package row previews, and template row previews are not live supplier-priced sources and are emitted only as ranking hints, review-required allowance rows, room/row pattern hints, or explicit reviewed template-row copies with source warnings; generic `sourceType: "template"` rows remain rejected by validation and Apply runtime guards outside the dedicated row-copy contract. Draft returns a normalized brief, project/estimate/tree/row/template/template-row-copy draft, component/template matches, marked allowance rows, budget summary, assumptions/warnings, operation eligibility, a server draft hash, and a server-signed HMAC draft token bound to the draft id/hash, user, workspace, provider/model, and expiry. Draft mode writes no production records, package-builder read tools must not call workspace-bootstrap helpers that can create/update workspace or profile rows during Draft, provider `searchTerms` do not authorize model-directed SQL or broad retrieval, and linked component rows must carry either a confirmed pr