.ai/03_plans/2026-06-12-Projects-Auto-Added-To-Templates/02_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md:176:- **Editor:** load only the active tab's tree. `getEstimateTabTree(estimateId, tabId)` filters nodes by `estimate_tab_id` (new index `(estimate_tab_id, parent_id, sort_order)`), rows by joining the tab's node ids — strictly less data per query than today's whole-estimate load. Tab list is a tiny separate query. Route-level load limits (1200/3000) become per-tab. **Budgets:** tab switch triggers at most one `tabs` read (if stale) + one `tabTree` read; no whole-estimate row fetch; a 1,200-node/3,000-row tab returns within the current route limit without raising the 413 ceiling; switching tabs must not render row tables from the previously active tab. EXPLAIN proof is required in implementation; hosted query plans remain **[M]** provider proof.
