.ai/03_plans/2026-06-12-Projects-Auto-Added-To-Templates/14_IMPLEMENTATION_HANDOFF.md:27:**Phase 1 (database tab foundation), authored and proven locally first** ([10](10_IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md) Phase 1; [03](03_DATABASE_MIGRATION_PLAN.md) §3–13). It is the safest first slice because: it is invisible to users (no app code reads tabs); it carries the project's only hard-to-reverse risk (constraint swap + validator update) and therefore deserves first, isolated attention with the proof harness (`scripts/prove-estimate-tabs-postgres.mjs`) before any UI exists; every later phase depends on it; and its rollback story is cleanest while nothing consumes the new schema. Note the repo's standing constraint: **agents have no hosted-DB channel** — local harness proof first; linked apply (`npx supabase@2.98.2 db push` + type regen) is owner-authorized separately.
