th `ai_package_apply_commands` replay semantics and transactional `create_cost_library_component` execution, bounded in-memory pre-Apply draft revision/refine with fresh signed hash/token, metadata-only rejected-draft feedback, a default-off accepted/rejected package-builder source-signal memory slice for deterministic ranking hints only, and post-Apply workspace handoffs built from server-returned Apply ids.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/README.md:32:- Draft mode builds a reviewable package draft from compact authenticated read-tool summaries plus optional DeepSeek structured hints and deterministic server-side fallback logic. The deterministic fallback now recognizes 3-bedroom condo/unit prompts, creates bedroom plus toilet/bath Area Nodes, folds in bounded matched template area names as structure hints, can reuse matched scoped library components for repeated requirements such as beds and wardrobes in bedrooms plus water closets and lavatories in toilet/bath areas, can use linked prior-project component usage as a ranking hint when choosing between otherwise similar scoped library components, can fan out Living/Dining rooms across multiple tightly matched scoped library components, can use matched prior estimate rows from accessible workspace projects as reviewed allowance precedents when live library components are missing, can use bounded matched estimate-template row previews as review-required allowance rows for package creation, and can build current-route direct template row-copy drafts through a separate `templateRowCopyDraft` contract. Draft read searches use the full bounded package vocabulary so generic condo prompts can still discover bedroom, wardrobe, kitchen, water-closet, lavatory/basin/sink/faucet, living, dining, furniture, console, table, sofa, chair, pendant, lounge, light, fixture, paint, tile, bathroom, sanitary, finish, and general app data before deterministic scoring. Generic rooms such as Living and Dining can now use multiple matched library rows first, then matched prior-project rows as reviewed allowance precedents before falling back to generated allowances. Provider `searchTerms` are normalized, capped, and used only as row-planning hints against already-retrieved scoped component matches; they do not authorize model-directed SQL or broad retrieval. Draft provider context may include bounded portfolio project labels and current project estimate summaries; when a prompt is sent from a project/estimate route it may also include provider-safe current project name, estimate summary, area names/paths, and compact current area rows. Raw project/estimate/node/row ids and client/location details are not sent to the provider.
