.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/README.md:37:- Pending Draft previews can be revised or rejected before Apply by sending the verified draft boundary. Additive follow-ups continue through `mode: "draft"` with base-draft fields so scoped library components can be appended to the pending draft. Deterministic cost/removal refinements use `mode: "refine"`, verify the same base hash/token before any read tools, skip provider generation, return a fresh draft/hash/token with `productionWrite: false`, and audit metadata as `mode: "draft"` with refinement/revision fields. Rejected previews, including server-signed previews that are not Apply-eligible, use `mode: "feedback"` with the reviewed draft/hash/token, verify the same signed boundary, record metadata-only rejected-draft feedback as `mode: "draft"` audit, call no read tools/provider/Apply path, and close the preview so it cannot be applied or revised. Old UI previews are marked stale so their Apply button cannot be used after a newer refined preview exists.
