.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:43:- Draft mode accepts package-building prompts such as "Assemble me a 3 bedroom package, budget is 5 million pesos", uses compact authenticated project/component/template/prior-row summaries when Supabase workspace auth is available, may ask DeepSeek for structured draft hints through the provider boundary, and falls back to deterministic server-side package assembly when the provider is unavailable or invalid. The deterministic fallback now recognizes 3-bedroom condo/unit prompts, names the draft "3 Bedroom Condo Unit", creates bedroom plus toilet/bath Area Nodes, folds bounded matched template area names into the draft structure, can reuse matched workspace library components for repeated needs such as beds and wardrobes in bedrooms plus water closets and lavatories in toilet/bath areas, can use matched prior estimate rows from accessible workspace projects as reviewed allowance precedents when live library components are missing, can use bounded matched estimate-template row previews as review-required allowance rows without enabling template-source row Apply, and can build current-route matched template-insert drafts for whole reusable-template copies into existing estimates. Draft read searches use a bounded package vocabulary so generic condo prompts can discover bedroom, wardrobe, kitchen, water-closet, lavatory/basin/sink/faucet, and finish-related app data before deterministic scoring.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:44:- Draft mode writes no production records. It returns a normalized package brief, project/estimate draft, Group/Area estimate tree draft, component/template match summaries, clearly marked allowance rows, budget summary, assumptions, warnings, operation eligibility, a server draft hash, and a server-signed HMAC draft token bound to draft id/hash, user, workspace, provider/model, and expiry. Package-builder read tools now read the workspace display context from the already server-derived `userContext.workspaceId` and must not call workspace bootstrap helpers that can create/update workspace or profile records during Draft. Linked component rows with a price option require the confirmed price-option `updated_at`; linked rows without a price option carry a component-version snapshot, and Apply rejects stale or missing freshness evidence before writing.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:51:- Memory/RAG remains disabled by default. A narrow package-builder memory slice is implemented behind `AI_PACKAGE_BUILDER_MEMORY_ENABLED`: accepted Apply and rejected feedback can record safe structured source signals for scoped library items/templates, read tools summarize those user/workspace-scoped signals, and deterministic Draft uses them only as ranking hints. Memory writes are best-effort, do not block feedback or Apply, do not authorize reads/writes, do not bypass freshness checks, and are not sent to the provider. The local migration `20260528103341_ai_package_builder_memory.sql` defines the memory table/RLS surface but has not been applied to the linked Supabase remote in this slice.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:52:- Historical estimate rows are bounded, audited, provider-minimized, and used only as precedent hints. They do not become linked supplier-priced rows; deterministic Draft emits them as review-required allowance rows with historical-precedent warnings unless a current library component match is available.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:53:- Comparable prior estimate packages are bounded, audited, provider-minimized, and used only as room/row/cost/source-coverage pattern hints. They can add matched prior-estimate area names to the Draft room program and emit reviewed allowance rows from comparable row previews, but they do not become linked supplier-priced rows or bypass Apply validation.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:68:- Ask provider context includes exact `projectCount` only for project-count questions, bounded project labels for project-list questions, compact ID-free component-library matches with active price-option unit/cost/currency values for component/library/price questions, compact ID-free reusable-template matches with bounded area names and row previews for template questions, compact ID-free historical estimate-row matches for prior-row/other-project usage questions, compact ID-free project chart bucket summaries for chart/cost-breakdown questions, validated current-route project and estimate labels for route-context questions, compact current-estimate tree/row/total context for current estimate questions, compact current-estimate activity summaries for activity/history/who-edited questions, and explicit guidance that retrieved text is untrusted data.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:70:- The server does not hardcode the natural-language project answer. It derives user/workspace, fetches compact context through app-owned reads, and lets the provider answer from that context while the server keeps authorization, minimization, and audit control.
.ai/03_plans/ai-chatbot-agent-readiness/12-implementation-slice-log.md:72:- Local admin DB bypass remains rejected before AI context resolution. Local dev auth bypass is rejected before AI provider calls so account-aware Ask/package-builder flows must use a real Supabase workspace session.
